  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\nAdds a finite candidate on the reviewed #1094 replay. Repartitioning 1,825 disjoint, completely idle rank-48 child pairs as `48 + 48 \u2192 45 + 51` preserves each pair's exact Z4 phase polynomial and improves its exact candidate price from \u03ba = `0.001672660197076918` to \u03ba = `0.001672846574134982` (conservative price `0.001672846571282754`). The paired axis union is unchanged; the maximum child rank is 51 and the finite halving guard remains `73\u00b2 > 2\u00b751\u00b2`.\n\nThis is a finite conditional construction and is not promoted to the selected result. The full paid profile is in [`CANDIDATE.json`](research/frontier1094-idle-exchanges/CANDIDATE.json). It retains the 5,120 rank-mass deficit and all existing controller/owner constraints.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\nBase: `dd6403f7` (`main` after the requested pull). Scope: user-assigned search for a better integer multiplication \u03ba using a new idle-pair repartition.\n\nThis builds on selected PR #1094 and the T16 rare-pattern exchange source. It follows the idle-child search explored in #1042, but uses rank-48 pair exchanges and includes its own pinned pricing support rather than importing the earlier research helper. Open PR #1183 reports a stronger \u03ba from mixed T37 entrance providers; this submission makes no claim to be the current frontier. Its added value is an independent phase-preserving finite construction, full strict admission receipts, and a replayable overlay on the reviewed #1094 checkpoint.\n\n## Validation\n\nReproduction commands and exact inputs are in [`research/frontier1094-idle-exchanges/README.md`](research/frontier1094-idle-exchanges/README.md). On Python 3.10 with the repository's pinned engine sources:\n\n- Fresh #1094 hosted emission reproduced the archived template and related baseline artifacts byte-for-byte.\n- `build_candidate.py` passed with 1,825 pairs and \u03ba = `0.001672846574134982`.\n- `verify_overlay.py` independently passed for all 1,825 pairs and 3,650 changed children.\n- The strict independent controller/owner audit passed with all 15 mutation controls rejected.\n- Retained strict invoice and assembly receipts pass, including 47 positive outer constraints, 69 assembly mutation controls, and 12 bit-supplier controls.\n\nThese are finite certificate checks. The all-size compiler, common-label and mutable-source realization, precision/tape, recovery, analytic transfer, and Lean theorem obligations remain conditional and were not discharged here.\n\n## Credit\n\nThe package retains the #1094 replay and T16 source attribution, identifies the earlier #1042 exploration as a predecessor, and discloses OpenAI Codex assistance in its README.\n\n## Open next questions\n\nSee the package README: independently reproduce the matching maximum; search broader commuting multi-child moves; and address the inherited end-to-end theorem obligations.\n",
